From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:31:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gbm: report YUV formats a driver can import

gbm_device_is_format_supported() answers only for the formats in the
visuals table, all RGB, so it reports NV12 unsupported even where the
driver imports NV12 dma-bufs, as EGL already does. Chromium on Wayland
asks it before importing a decoded video frame for a hardware overlay
(gbm_wrapper's GetSupportedGbmFlags), so on Mesa no VA-API frame can
become an overlay: the import is refused, the swap fails and the GPU
process restarts.

For a format without a visual, answer from the driver's dma-buf format
list, as for any other format, unless the use includes rendering or
the cursor, which need a visual.
---
 src/gbm/backends/dri/gbm_dri.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gbm/backends/dri/gbm_dri.c b/src/gbm/backends/dri/gbm_dri.c
index 316b251..91f2be4 100644
--- a/src/gbm/backends/dri/gbm_dri.c
+++ b/src/gbm/backends/dri/gbm_dri.c
@@ -353,7 +353,11 @@ gbm_dri_is_format_supported(struct gbm_device *gbm,
       return 0;
 
    format = core->v0.format_canonicalize(format);
-   if (gbm_format_to_pipe_format(format) == 0)
+   /* A format without a visual, such as YUV, is never rendered to, but the
+    * driver may still import it: its dma-buf formats answer the other uses. */
+   if (gbm_format_to_pipe_format(format) == 0 &&
+       (!dri->has_dmabuf_import ||
+        (usage & (GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING | GBM_BO_USE_CURSOR))))
       return 0;
 
    /* If there is no query, fall back to the small table which was originally
